<workout_file><author>mywhooshinfo.com</author><name>Champs-Elysees</name><description>Perhaps the most famous road for any sprinter, the Champs-Elysees, indeed the most coveted victory you could have as a sprinter. Winning the final stage of the Tour de France, in Paris, on this famous 1.9Km section of the cobbled avenue. 

As we head into the preparation phase of this Sprint Focussed Programme, we simulate the final stage of the Tour de France with a series of strenuous efforts, culminating in a sprint for the win!</description><sportType>bike</sportType><workout>
<SteadyState  Duration="240" Power="0.5"><textevent timeoffset="0" message="The warm up is a good routine to get into the habit of. "/><textevent timeoffset="20" message="Starting easy"/><textevent timeoffset="30" message="traditionally the final stage of the Tour de France is a procession"/><textevent timeoffset="40" message="With an opportunity for the teams to take photos"/><textevent timeoffset="50" message="Toast some champagne and celebrate an amazing feat of endurance"/><textevent timeoffset="60" message="The general classification has usually been decided"/><textevent timeoffset="70" message="And all that is left is to decide the final sprint"/><textevent timeoffset="80" message="The stage is typically a short one"/><textevent timeoffset="90" message="Starting outside of Paris"/><textevent timeoffset="100" message="And finishing in the shadow of the Arc de Triomphe"/><textevent timeoffset="110" message="Usually 8 complete laps of the finishing circuit of around 7 Km"/><textevent timeoffset="120" message="Today however, we will jump in for the final few laps"/><textevent timeoffset="130" message="At this point chaos ensues"/><textevent timeoffset="140" message="With attacks from teams without a sprinter"/><textevent timeoffset="150" message="Whilst the sprint teams try to control the race"/></SteadyState>
<SteadyState  Duration="180" Power="0.64999997615814"><textevent timeoffset="0" message="Progressing through the zones,"/><textevent timeoffset="20" message="to ensure you are prepared for the race to come."/></SteadyState>
<SteadyState  Cadence="75" Duration="180" Power="0.83999997377396"><textevent timeoffset="0" message="Lower your cadence and increase the gear to raise the power here!"/></SteadyState>
<SteadyState  Duration="120" Power="1"><textevent timeoffset="0" message="This effort is to ensure you kick-start your oxygen carrying capacity and utilisation. If your legs are hurting by now, it is NOT a bad thing! "/></SteadyState>
<SteadyState  Duration="180" Power="0.5"><textevent timeoffset="0" message="3 minute easy before some sprints to prime the legs"/></SteadyState>
<SteadyState  Duration="10" Power="2"><textevent timeoffset="0" message="Full-Gas, like you are sprinting for the finish line!!! "/></SteadyState>
<SteadyState  Duration="50" Power="0.5"><textevent timeoffset="0" message="Catch your breath..."/></SteadyState>
<SteadyState  Duration="10" Power="2"><textevent timeoffset="0" message="Full-Gas, like you are sprinting for the finish line!!! "/></SteadyState>
<SteadyState  Duration="50" Power="0.5"><textevent timeoffset="0" message="Catch your breath..."/></SteadyState>
<SteadyState  Duration="120" Power="0.5"><textevent timeoffset="20" message="The shorter the race/event, the longer and more intense the warm up should be"/><textevent timeoffset="40" message="Getting ready to jump into the race"/><textevent timeoffset="60" message="You should be well warmed up now"/></SteadyState>
<SteadyState  Duration="300" Power="0.94999998807907"><textevent timeoffset="30" message="Starting with a fast pace as riders try and go for the break. "/><textevent timeoffset="50" message="As we get towards the final few circuits, there will be big attacks"/><textevent timeoffset="70" message="We have to follow them all"/><textevent timeoffset="90" message="As having a breakaway go at this point in the race is dangerous"/><textevent timeoffset="110" message="Don&#039;t worry, your team will do most of the work, you just have to follow"/><textevent timeoffset="130" message="Sounds easy right..."/><textevent timeoffset="150" message="Not quite!"/><textevent timeoffset="200" message="There is a drag up to the Arc de Triomphe after the finish line"/><textevent timeoffset="230" message="It is always a launch pad for attacks"/><textevent timeoffset="260" message="And will get more and more difficult with each lap"/><textevent timeoffset="290" message="On the cobbles it is double as tough on the body"/></SteadyState>
<SteadyState  Duration="180" Power="1.2000000476837"><textevent timeoffset="0" message="If the selection of riders in the break is not ideal we will need to bring it back. "/><textevent timeoffset="60" message="Here you have to press on"/><textevent timeoffset="90" message="It is a dangerous group of riders"/></SteadyState>
<SteadyState  Duration="180" Power="0.5"><textevent timeoffset="0" message="Good job, brought it back "/><textevent timeoffset="60" message="A slight lull as we come down the back straight of the circuit"/></SteadyState>
<SteadyState  Duration="240" Power="0.94999998807907"><textevent timeoffset="0" message="With an intermediate sprint coming up, the sprinters teams start to place themselves at the head of the field"/><textevent timeoffset="30" message="the intermediate sprint is on the back straight"/><textevent timeoffset="60" message="It will be fast after the finish line"/><textevent timeoffset="80" message="Then the roundabout"/><textevent timeoffset="100" message="then the small sprint"/><textevent timeoffset="150" message="just follow the wheels in the sprint, we are focussing on the final"/></SteadyState>
<SteadyState  Duration="120" Power="1.2000000476837"><textevent timeoffset="0" message="The pace is ramping up, we are sprinting straight after this effort with loaded legs. "/><textevent timeoffset="30" message="Pick up the cadence here"/><textevent timeoffset="60" message="This should be a speed sprint"/><textevent timeoffset="90" message="high cadence, slightly lower power"/></SteadyState>
<SteadyState  Duration="10" Power="1.7000000476837"><textevent timeoffset="0" message="Sprint to follow the wheels "/></SteadyState>
<SteadyState  Duration="300" Power="0.55000001192093"><textevent timeoffset="0" message="Good job"/><textevent timeoffset="30" message="Another lull in the peloton"/><textevent timeoffset="60" message="No one is breaking away now"/><textevent timeoffset="90" message="Take this moment to drink and relax a bit"/><textevent timeoffset="150" message="But not too much, it could kick off at any moment"/></SteadyState>
<SteadyState  Duration="10" Power="2"><textevent timeoffset="0" message="Sprint for Position"/></SteadyState>
<SteadyState  Duration="120" Power="0.60000002384186"><textevent timeoffset="0" message="Sprint stages are often a series of max efforts to get in position"/><textevent timeoffset="30" message="especially on this coveted stage"/><textevent timeoffset="60" message="nerves are running high"/></SteadyState>
<SteadyState  Duration="10" Power="1.7000000476837"><textevent timeoffset="0" message="We go again!"/></SteadyState>
<SteadyState  Duration="180" Power="0.60000002384186"><textevent timeoffset="0" message="Ok, final few Km of the stage, "/><textevent timeoffset="30" message="there are lots of changes in pace here,"/><textevent timeoffset="60" message="so be sure to pay attention!"/></SteadyState>
<SteadyState  Duration="120" Power="0.85000002384186"><textevent timeoffset="0" message="Starting to ramp up, an effort to come. "/><textevent timeoffset="30" message="As the last gasp attacks go"/><textevent timeoffset="60" message="Hold a good cadence"/><textevent timeoffset="90" message="Stay seated"/></SteadyState>
<SteadyState  Duration="30" Power="1.5"><textevent timeoffset="0" message="In the final few Km the pace is often full of surges."/><textevent timeoffset="20" message="Push to hold your position"/></SteadyState>
<SteadyState  Duration="120" Power="0.91000002622604"><textevent timeoffset="0" message="Ramping up!"/><textevent timeoffset="20" message="Come on, hold on"/><textevent timeoffset="60" message="Last race of the Tour de France"/></SteadyState>
<SteadyState  Duration="120" Power="0.94999998807907"><textevent timeoffset="0" message="Final Km of the stage, get ready to unleash the Watts for the sprint finish."/><textevent timeoffset="60" message="Imagine crossing the line first, in Paris!"/></SteadyState>
<SteadyState  Duration="10" Power="1.0499999523163"><textevent timeoffset="0" message="300m to go, the sprint is coming!"/></SteadyState>
<SteadyState  Duration="10" Power="2.0999999046326"><textevent timeoffset="0" message="GO-GO-GO "/></SteadyState>
<SteadyState  Duration="400" Power="0.5"><textevent timeoffset="0" message="Great job! Be sure to practice your sprint technique, especially when fatigued. "/><textevent timeoffset="90" message="That was a great session"/><textevent timeoffset="120" message="A combination of everything that we have worked on in the Sprint Plan"/><textevent timeoffset="150" message="With some steady state efforts"/><textevent timeoffset="200" message="Short, anaerobic work"/><textevent timeoffset="220" message="And high power, high speed sprints"/><textevent timeoffset="300" message="Spin nice and easy for the remainder"/><textevent timeoffset="350" message="Catch your breath"/></SteadyState>
</workout></workout_file>